==Strategy==
This stage itself is an exact copy of [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]]. However, this stage has the nasty restriction of only allowing Normal Cats, Special Cats, Uber Rare Cats, and Legend Rare Cats to be deployed onto the battlefield. This restriction will make a huge difference in battle as very useful units on the Super Rare and Rare rarity such as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] can no longer be used, so having a high leveled up [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] or his [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l counterpart]] is pretty much mandatory if the player wants to beat the stage, unless you have some Anti-Red [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] of course. [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]], for example, can be stacked up at the start of the level to freeze Bore, and if you are lucky and time the Thunderbolt Cannon, can permafreeze Hannya.

Thankfully, as the years have gone by, a lot of stuff has been added in order to make this stage easier. Units such as [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]], [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]] with [[Talents]], [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] with [[Talents]], and [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] with [[Talents]] have assisted in powercreeping this stage, and should be considered.

A baseline strategy for this stage is slowly chipping down [[Hannya]] with a boosted [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] while also bursting down the threats such as [[Bore]] with [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] or any Anti Red alternatives the player might have. The [[R.Ost]], like in the original [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]] should be lured to your base to be chained by [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]. If the player fails to kill the [[R.Ost]] (such as the [[R.Ost]] or [[Hannya]] killing [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]), the player must use units such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] to kill the presumably low [[R.Ost]]. Do this for multiple cycles and you will beat this horrifying stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]: A very powerful option against Bore and Hannya that every player should have up to this point. Usefulness depends on levels, but around level 20+30 should likely be fine.

[[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)| Li'l Island Cat]]: While this unit has less stats than regular Island Cat, using both together can be a good solution to the Bore and killing Hannya without taking forever. Level 50 is also recommended, but you only need 10 plus levels if you level this unit to level 40 with catseyes.

[[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Dark Lazer]]: Completely annhilates this stage. Attack-Up talent is the only one you need for Bore, but defense lets Dark Lazer survive extra Hannya hits and Bore hits, while wave does chip damage to Hannya and knockbacks Ginger Snache. Defense talent even allows this unit to handle R.Ost by themselves, as long as he doesn't crit every attack. As long as you can bring a unit to kill Hannya (like Island), having Talented Dark Lazer will make this stage a complete joke.

[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: This is your R.Ost counter, assuming you don't bring talented Dark Lazer or ubers instead. Look at the 3rd video in the Walkthrough section for a guide on Bahamut Chaining.

